@Andrew -- Making all the take-out letters "A" would have been terrific.  So would making the take-out letters spell something related to the revealer (GAPE?).  

I'm guessing that it was hard enough to get the answers to cross before adding another condition to the theme answers, and that maybe there aren't four pairs of answers where a double-A removal was possible, nor that the take-out letters could spell a related word.

Sometimes reality doesn't conform.  Meanwhile, I found it quite impressive in any case that the theme pairs crossed.

